title repeat_conic_paint -- the repeating conic gradient, the sweep that tiles, GREEN
prompt Read crux/REMEMBER and the road-ahead docs; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; each lap deep-read one council-rota doc; send often; stop at custody gates. baton prin recur
think The CSS gradient family in image/ had five of six shapes -- linear (gradient_paint), radial (radial_paint), conic (conic_paint), repeating-linear (repeat_paint), repeating-radial (repeat_radial_paint). The one missing member is repeating-conic. Completing a bounded family is the highest-Lindy crux available: it closes a set a surface can rely on rather than opening a sixth loose thread, and it composes with the exact three public APIs the family already stands on (color_ramp_stops decides, qoi owns the target, color composites) -- no new color math, no new codec.
think Council rota lap index 11 (git rev count 38351 mod 27) -> active-designing/yonder/20260618-182412_single-stranded.md, deep-read. Its lens fit the work exactly: simple over easy, each part about one thing, composed not braided. repeat_conic_paint is single-stranded -- it only ROUTES a pixel to its tiled angular bearing; the color decision, the RGBA target, and the compositing each stay their own free module. No seam is no braid.
think Routing reuses conic_paint's doubled-coordinate pseudo-angle (four quadrants clockwise from the top, position growing with the ratio of the two doubled coords) but keeps the bearing at FULL precision as the turn fraction T/D (T = q*s + numer, D = 4*s) before quantizing, so tiling can wind it cleanly: tile = (T*reps) mod D, scaled tile*pos_max/D. Holding T/D exact rather than the u8 bearing is the crux that makes the modulo land on clean tile boundaries.
think Bounds: s = |dx2|+|dy2| <= ~16382, T < 4*s <= ~65528, reps <= qoi_max_dim, so T*reps <= ~5.4e8 and tile*pos_max <= ~1.7e7 -- both far inside u64, no wrap. Named refusals up front: BadStripDims, StripTooSmall (single pixel), RepsTooSmall (reps<2, which is the plain conic), RepsTooLarge (>qoi_max_dim), RepeatConicOutOfBounds, plus every color_ramp_stops refusal -- all before any pixel, so a refusal paints nothing (proven by re-scanning all-white).
think Made exact by a black->white ramp on an odd 7x7 box, reps 2, center (3,3): the top reads 0, east 127, south 0, west 127 -- the ramp cycles twice around the turn, so top and south share the first control and east and west the mid, a repeat the single conic (0,63,127,191) can never make. A cell just clockwise of the south seam reads 223 before south drops to 0 (a hard seam); reps 4 wraps the east bearing to 0 where reps 2 read 127 (the winding count is a real control).
obs GREEN on the FIRST build and first witness run -- the hand-computed cardinal bearings (top 0, east 127, south 0, west 127 at reps 2) and the seam pixel (4,6)=223 all matched metal. tame_style_check bans clean, width-check exit 0, plain 7-bit ASCII, >= 2 positive asserts per fn.
obs The six-member CSS gradient family is now whole in Rye: linear, radial, conic, and each of their repeating twins, every one witnessed byte-for-byte through the open QOI codec. A surface (Skate, Realidream, Photos) can now name any CSS gradient shape and read back a real image, on our own color model, floor code that waits on no design system.
loom witness=repeat_conic_paint_witness green=1 box=7x7 reps=2 bearing=full-precision-turn-fraction
file image/repeat_conic_paint.rye the repeating conic gradient -- winds the ramp reps times around the turn and tiles it as hard-seamed pie wedges, bearing held at full precision then wound and reduced
file tools/repeat_conic_paint_witness.rish proves the tiling, hard seam, constant wedges, reps control, and QOI round trip on metal; GREEN first run
file image/README.md names repeat_conic_paint.rye beside repeat_radial_paint.rye, calling it the sixth and last of the family (docs-sync)
recommend keep-going the CSS gradient family is complete; the next Season G crux is a gradient-as-fill compose (paint a gradient into a shape mask) or the open-fonts glyph codec journey -- all agent-doable, no gate
